# G-code post-processor fixtures are byte-exact machine files. Their line
# endings ARE the thing under test (the EVO49 needs CRLF; the known-broken
# fixture is deliberately LF-only), so git must never normalise them.
# Without this, core.autocrlf=true rewrites them on commit/checkout and the
# encoding tests pass or fail for the wrong reason.
src/lib/optimiser/__tests__/fixtures/gcode/** -text
